  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive services and opportunities for the host communities and displaced Rohingya population project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rohingya population and adjacent host communities face a multitude of health challenges, including high rates of morbidity, limited access to essential medicines and treatment, susceptibility to infectious diseases and natural disasters, with critical challenges in healthcare infrastructure and healthcare workers. The project aims to reduce health-related vulnerabilities of Rohingya Refugees in Cox&apos;s Bazar and Bhasan Char and host Communities through the provision of quality and comprehensive essential healthcare services with preparedness and response measures for public health emergencies. This will (1) Enhance equitable access to essential primary and secondary healthcare services by operating 18 health facilities, emergency referral support system and community-based health interventions, (2) Enhance resilience to communicable disease outbreaks, disasters and other public health emergencies through robust preparedness, prevention, and response measures, (3) Improve access to integrated mental health and psychosocial services at individual and community level, (4) Adapted health facilities to prevent and/or withstand public health emergencies and climate hazards, (5) Establish an efficient medicine supply chain system to improve availability of and access to essential medicines. This project also seeks to strengthen the government health system in Cox&apos;s Bazar district through the provision of qualified medical and support staffs to selected health facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
